{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "&lt;p&gt;The development shall be operated in accordance with the hereby approved Fire Safety Strategy for Brockley Hill Farm (received 21.11.23) in perpetuity (unless otherwise agreed in writing with the LPA).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 2015 (or any order revoking and re-enacting that order with or without modification) and any further restrictions arising from being within the curtilage of a Listed Building , no development which would otherwise fall within Classes A, AA through to I (inclusive) of Part 1 of Schedule 2 to that Order shall be carried out in regard to the dwellinghouses hereby permitted, without the prior written permission of the local planning authority.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The occupation of the dwelling hereby approved shall be limited to a person(s) solely or mainly working, in agriculture as defined by section 336 (1) of the 1990 Town and Country Planning Act (as amended) on Brockley Hill Farm (the area outlined in red on the Location Plan attached to this application and to any resident dependants.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The conversion / expansion of the barn as an ancillary residential unit hereby permitted shall not be occupied or used at any time as a separate residential unit and shall remain in an ancillary use to the host dwellinghouse/farmhouse at Brockley Hill Farm, Brockley Hill, Stanmore HA7 4LN. Any other material change of use would require planning permission.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;",
    "The materials and finish to be used in the fenestration changes hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing or adjacent walls (unless otherwise agreed in writing).&amp;nbsp;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed rooflights shall, as far as is possible, be flush with the roofslope (conservation grade rooflights). The barn doors shown on both north and south elevations (potentially hiding further fenestration) shall be provided / retained as shown.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;Any additional external lighting on the converted barn or associated with its residential usage shall conform to the following points (unless otherwise agreed in writing):&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;All lighting will point downwards.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Cowls will be fitted to ensure no light spill into the woodland or sky.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Lighting will be movement sensitive to ensure the lights are on for the minimum period.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The lighting will comprise LEDs in the warm white spectrum at 2700K or less.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Lighting levels should not exceed 1 Lux at the woodland edge.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Any other measures and methodology identified within the recommendation of the approved Preliminary Roosting Assessment relating to future lighting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;[Site] Location Plan; B0724-1 - Site Survey; BH-02-101 - Existing Plans and Elevations [farmhouse]; BH-02-102 - Existing Plans and Elevations; BH-02-103 - Proposed Plans and Elevations; Planning Fire Strategy (received 22.11.24); Flood Risk Assessment / Briefing Note (received 12.12.24); Design and Access Statement (received 05.07.24); Preliminary Roosting Assessment&amp;nbsp;by MMEnvironmental Ltd (dated 18 August 2024)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;All plans received 04.09.24 unless otherwise stated&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
